a; Europe, Middle East, and Africa; and Asia. Adient plc was incorporated in 2016 and is based in Dublin, Ireland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jerome J. Dorlack | President, CEO & Director | Age 44 | Compensation: $2.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Adient plc is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $1.2B market cap on $14.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 2% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 6% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $204M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -8.2% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 12.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 10.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 8% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 62/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 76% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 62% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Research Analysts\u2019 Price Target Changes for November 6th (ABNB, ADNT, ALL, AMC, AMPL, APTV, BDX, BROS, CAVA, ET)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/research-analysts-price-target-changes-for-november-6th-abnb-adnt-all-amc-ampl-aptv-bdx-bros-cava-et.html","date"